 ## Non-negotiable invariants
 - Qualification is external evidence bound to the exact immutable descriptor digest; PLATFORM-009 never self-qualifies a model.
+- Descriptor registration is idempotent only by exact descriptor identity: JDBC replay conflicts on `descriptor_id`, then verifies the stored canonical descriptor digest before accepting replay.
 - Moving aliases cannot hold QUALIFIED standing. Model/provider/version/artifact/configuration/endpoint/backend identity is exact.
 - Qualification history is append-only; current standing may advance only with later evaluation evidence. Material descriptor change requires new qualification.
 - Context projection is digest-bound, expiring, trust-labelled and secret-minimized. Retrieved/tool/file content remains untrusted DATA and cannot become instruction authority.
